<% content_for :title, "NEET PG Choice Planner" %>
<% content_for :body_class, "landing" %>
<header class="lp-nav">
  <span class="lp-brand">NEET PG Choice Planner</span>
  <nav>
    <%= link_to "Extension", extension_path %>
    <%= link_to "https://github.com/fazzledev/neet-pg-choice-planner", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener", "aria-label": "Source on GitHub" do %><%= icon("github") %><% end %>
    <%= link_to "Open planner", planner_path, class: "button primary" %>
  </nav>
</header>

<main class="lp">
  <section class="lp-hero">
    <span class="lp-kicker">NEET PG 2026 counselling</span>
    <h1>Plan your choices calmly.<br>Then fill them in minutes.</h1>
    <p class="lp-lede">Search all <%= number_with_delimiter(@choice_count) %> choices across <%= number_with_delimiter(@institute_count) %> institutes, shape your plan the way you think, and copy it to the counselling portal in one click.</p>
    <div class="lp-cta">
      <%= link_to planner_path, class: "button primary lp-big" do %>Start planning<%= icon("arrow-right") %><% end %>
      <%= link_to extension_path, class: "button lp-big" do %><%= icon("puzzle") %>Get the filler extension<% end %>
    </div>
    <p class="lp-note"><%= icon("shield-check") %>Free and open source. No account needed. Works offline.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="lp-section">
    <h2>Everything the portal makes hard</h2>
    <div class="lp-grid">
      <article class="lp-card">
        <span class="lp-icon"><%= icon("search") %></span>
        <h3>Find seats fast</h3>
        <p>Search by college, city or speciality. Filter by course, state, institute type and quota, with as many picks per filter as you like.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="lp-card">
        <span class="lp-icon"><%= icon("layers") %></span>
        <h3>Group the way you think</h3>
        <p>See the catalog and your plan grouped by institute or by speciality, so you can compare options side by side.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="lp-card">
        <span class="lp-icon"><%= icon("grip-vertical") %></span>
        <h3>Drag to rank</h3>
        <p>Reorder by dragging or by typing a rank, gather a college's seats together, and keep a note on every choice.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="lp-card">
        <span class="lp-icon"><%= icon("wifi-off") %></span>
        <h3>Works offline</h3>
        <p>Your plan is saved in your browser as you go. A dropped connection or a portal outage costs you nothing.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="lp-card">
        <span class="lp-icon"><%= icon("cloud") %></span>
        <h3>Sync and undo</h3>
        <p>Sign in with an emailed link to use the same plan on phone and laptop, with a history you can restore from.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="lp-card">
        <span class="lp-icon"><%= icon("phone") %></span>
        <h3>Ask before you choose</h3>
        <p>For shortlisted DNB hospitals, the coordinator's contact sits next to the seat, so you can ask about stipend, bond and duty hours first.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="lp-section lp-split">
    <div>
      <span class="lp-kicker">Chrome extension</span>
      <h2>Copy your plan to the portal</h2>
<p>Plan in Choice Planner, then let the extension make the counselling portal match. It works in Chrome on a computer.</p>
      <ol class="lp-steps">
        <li>Open the planner in Chrome. Your plan syncs to the extension by itself.</li>
        <li>Sign in to the counselling portal yourself and open Choice Filling. The panel says <em>In sync</em> or how many choices differ.</li>
        <li>Press <strong>Plan → MCC</strong>. MCC becomes an exact copy of your plan: missing choices added, dropped ones removed, everything in your order of preference. Check it, then press Save and Continue and enter the OTP.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Changed your list on the portal directly? <strong>MCC → Plan</strong> makes your plan a copy of MCC instead, and you can undo it.</p>
      <%= link_to extension_path, class: "button lp-big" do %><%= icon("download") %>Install the extension<% end %>
    </div>
    <figure class="lp-panel" aria-label="Example of the extension panel">
      <strong>NEET PG Choice Planner</strong>
      <p class="lp-panel-sub">Your plan: 60 choices, synced just now.</p>
      <p class="lp-panel-state">3 differences</p>
      <div class="lp-panel-group missing">
        <h4>In your plan, not on MCC yet (2)</h4>
        <p><span>#14</span>Aster Medcity, Kochi · Orthopaedics · DNB Quota</p>
        <p><span>#15</span>Lisie Hospital, Kochi · Orthopaedics · DNB Quota</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-panel-group moved">
        <h4>On MCC at a different rank (1)</h4>
        <p><span>MCC #9</span>Govt. Medical College, Kozhikode · M.S. Orthopaedics</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-panel-actions"><span class="lp-panel-btn">Plan → MCC</span><span class="lp-panel-btn ghost">MCC → Plan</span></div>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="lp-section lp-trust">
    <h2>You stay in control</h2>
    <div class="lp-grid three">
      <article class="lp-card">
        <span class="lp-icon"><%= icon("shield-check") %></span>
        <h3>Never locks</h3>
        <p>The extension refuses anything that locks choices. Saving and locking stay with you.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="lp-card">
        <span class="lp-icon"><%= icon("eye") %></span>
        <h3>Never signs in for you</h3>
        <p>You type your portal password, pin and OTP. Choice Planner never sees them.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="lp-card">
        <span class="lp-icon"><%= icon("github") %></span>
        <h3>Open source</h3>
        <p>Every line is on GitHub under the MIT license, so anyone can check what it does.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="lp-final">
    <h2>Your plan, ready before the round opens</h2>
    <%= link_to planner_path, class: "button primary lp-big" do %>Start planning<%= icon("arrow-right") %><% end %>
  </section>
</main>

<footer class="lp-foot">
  <p>NEET PG Choice Planner is an independent tool and is not affiliated with the Medical Counselling Committee, NBEMS or the Government of India. Choice data comes from the lists the Medical Counselling Committee publishes; always confirm on the official portal before locking.</p>
  <p>Built with ❤️, 🧠 and 🤖 by <%= link_to "Syed Fazil Basheer", "https://fazzle.dev", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %> · <%= link_to "Source on GitHub", "https://github.com/fazzledev/neet-pg-choice-planner", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %> · MIT license</p>
</footer>
